{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Mr Daley, in you come. Quick blood pressure before the doctor, 132 over 84, and your pulse is 76.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Cheers. Took forever to park, some bloke in a ute across two spots, and the freeway was a car park at the bridge.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Doctor's ready. Straight through.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (DOCTOR): G'day, I'm Dr Nguyen. Grab a seat. What's brought you in?",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): It's a lump. Down in the groin. I thought it was the left at first, well actually no, it's the right side. Pops out when I'm lifting and then it goes away.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Work's been flat out, pallets of tiles off the truck all week. Did you catch the cricket last night? Smith was set and then he nicked one and the whole pub went dead quiet. My brother-in-law reckons the bowling was—",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sorry, cutting in. When you lie down, is the lump still there?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Nah, it vanishes. I'm flat on the couch after tea and I can't find it. By the evening there's a mild ache, just a niggle, doesn't stop me sleeping.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any vomiting with it?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm, well, the weather this arvo, they're saying it'll bucket down and I left the ute windows—",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Sorry. Vomiting. No. I haven't vomited.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any fever? Does the area feel hot?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): No fever. Doesn't feel hot. Just that ache later on.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (DOCTOR): What do you actually do for work?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): Labouring. Shifting pallets of tiles, bit of signalling for the crane. On my feet the whole day.",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any regular medicines?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Only Panadol. Two of the 500 milligram tablets at night if the ache is playing up. Not every night, err, a few nights a week.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (DOCTOR): And reactions to drugs? Antibiotics or painkillers, anything that's disagreed with you?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, penacillin. I'm allergic. I get hives all over and my throat goes tight. They told me never to have it again.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (DOCTOR): Alright, penicillin is off the list, hives and a tight throat. Let me examine you. Stand up and cough.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): There's a soft swelling in the right groin, it bulges when you cough. Lie back for me. Yes, it slips back in. Not tender when I press.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): My granddaughter's got her school concert Friday, recorder of all things. The dog hides under the couch when she practises. I was hoping I can still go.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (DOCTOR): You should make the concert. Thinking it through, lump on lifting, gone when you lie down, cough impulse, reduces. This is behaving like an inguinal hernia. That's my working impression, not a final say.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): So is it dangerous? I've got a big job next week and the boss—",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (DOCTOR): Not an emergency today, from what I can feel. I'll refer you to the surgical clinic and they'll talk about repairing it.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Right. Do I keep working normal?",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (DOCTOR): Ease off the heavy lifting until the surgeons have seen you. If a pallet has to move, get a mate on it, don't do it yourself.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, I'll tell the boss. He won't be thrilled.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): If the lump won't go back in, or you start vomiting, or the pain turns severe, come straight back or go to emergency.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): And the Panadol, keep that up?",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): Yes. Two 500 milligram tablets at night when it aches is fine. Paracetamol isn't related to penicillin.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): I'll have the surgical referral sent from the desk as you leave.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): Beauty. Thanks for that."
 ],
